<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6496" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cănīcŭla</span></b> ,
		ae, f.
		dim.
		canis. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A small dog or bitch</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 32, 7,
				26, § 79</span></i>.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, of a passionate, quarrelsome woman,
				<i><span class="en">Plaut.
				Curc. 5, 1, 8</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Gell. 4, 20,
			3</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b> Canis Minor, <i>the lesser dogstar</i>, <i>in the
				mouth of the constellation</i> Canis, q. v., <i><span class="en">Plin. 2, 47,
				47, § 123</span></i>; <i><span class="en">18, 28, 68, §
			268</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">flagrans,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					C. 3, 13, 9</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">flammans,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Manil. 5, 207</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rubra,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					S. 2, 5, 39</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sitiens,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. A.
					A. 2, 231</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">insana,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Pers. 3,
					5</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">caniculae aestus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					C. 1, 17, 17</span></i>
			.—<b>Trop.</b>, of Diogenes: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">illa canicula Diogenes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. adv. Marc. 11</span></i>
			; cf. capella.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>A kind of sea-dog</i> (cf. canis, II. B.), <i><span class="en">Plin. 9,
				46, 70, § 151 sq.</span></i>—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>C.</b>
			<i>The worst throw with dice</i>, <i>the
				dog throw;</i> opp. to Venus (v. canis, II. C., and alea),
				<i><span class="en">Pers.
				3, 49</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
